.\" CLI synopsis generated by help2man; configuration sections maintained with the source.
.TH SPINE "1" "October 10, 2026" "SPINE 1.3.0  Copyright 2004-2026 by The Cacti Group" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
SPINE \- Data Collector for Cacti
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spine
[\fI\,options\/\fR] [[\fI\,firstid lastid\/\fR] \fI\,||
\/\fR[\fI\,-H/--hostlist='hostid1,hostid2,\/\fR...\fI\,,hostidn'\/\fR]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
SPINE 1.3.0  Copyright 2004\-2026 by The Cacti Group
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR/\-\-help
Show this brief help listing
.TP
\fB\-f\fR/\-\-first=X
Start polling with host id X
.TP
\fB\-l\fR/\-\-last=X
End polling with host id X
.TP
\fB\-H\fR/\-\-hostlist=X
Poll the list of host ids, separated by comma's
.TP
\fB\-p\fR/\-\-poller=X
Set the poller id to X
.TP
\fB\-t\fR/\-\-threads=X
Override the database threads setting.
.TP
\fB\-C\fR/\-\-conf=F
Read spine configuration from file F
.TP
\fB\-O\fR/\-\-option=S:V
Override DB settings 'set' with value 'V'
.TP
\fB\-M\fR/\-\-mibs
Refresh the device System Mib data
.TP
\fB\-N\fR/\-\-mode=online
For remote pollers, the operating mode.
Options include: online, offline, recovery.
The default is 'online'.
.TP
\fB\-R\fR/\-\-readonly
Spine will not write output to the DB
.TP
\fB\-S\fR/\-\-stdout
Logging is performed to standard output
.TP
\fB\-P\fR/\-\-pingonly
Ping device and update device status only
.TP
\fB\-V\fR/\-\-verbosity=V
Set logging verbosity to <V>
.PP
Either both of \fB\-\-first\fR/\-\-last must be provided, a valid hostlist must
be provided.
In their absence, all hosts are processed.
.SS "Without the --conf parameter, spine searches in order:"
.IP
current directory, /etc/, /etc/cacti/, ../etc/ for spine.conf.
.PP
Verbosity is one of NONE/LOW/MEDIUM/HIGH/DEBUG or 1..5
.PP
Runtime options are read from the 'settings' table in the Cacti
database, but they can be overridden with the \fB\-\-option\fR=\fI\,S\/\fR:V
parameter.
.SH EXTERNAL SCRIPT LIMITS
The following spine.conf directives apply to external commands, not the
persistent
PHP script server. All default to 0 (disabled). The database script_timeout
remains
the wall-clock deadline; a CPU limit does not replace it.
.TP
.B ScriptMaxOutputBytes
Maximum total stdout bytes, from 1 through RESULTS_BUFFER minus 1.
With any limit enabled, Spine reads until EOF within the wall-clock deadline.
Excess output, empty output, an unfinished command, or a failed limited child
produces an undefined result. The legacy single-read behavior remains when all
limits are disabled.
.TP
.B ScriptCpuSeconds
Per-process CPU-time limit in whole seconds, inherited by descendants.
The resource helper only lowers inherited soft and hard limits. This is not an
aggregate CPU budget for a process group.
.TP
.B ScriptMemoryMB
Per-process virtual address-space limit in MiB using Linux RLIMIT_AS.
Nonzero values are rejected on other platforms. This is not an RSS or aggregate
descendant-memory limit.
.PP
Values must be nonnegative decimal integers. Invalid or unsupported configured
limits fail startup. A missing resource helper fails command submission.
Timeouts and output breaches terminate the owned process group. Diagnostics
identify the device and data source without printing command arguments.
.SH SNMPV3 CONCURRENCY
SNMPv3 transactions share a lock with session construction and cleanup because
Net-SNMP USM state is shared. Configured network timeouts hold that lock; slow
or
unreachable v3 devices can delay healthy devices. SNMPv1/v2c requests retain
their
independent concurrent sessions. Polling worker defaults are unchanged.
.SH DATABASE COMPATIBILITY
Output, Boost output, and remote status transfers choose upsert syntax using the
actual destination connection. MySQL 8.0.19 and later use inserted-row aliases;
MariaDB and older or unidentified servers retain the VALUES(column) form.
Local and remote database capabilities are evaluated independently.
